  "event_order": [
    "Each GetInventoryValue invocation reads a selected packed two-bit slot and returns its current value. Each SetInventoryValue invocation replaces the selected slot and returns its previous value.",
    "Original GiveItem in src/itemUtils.c reads GetInventoryValue(item) before its branch; when the item is not a bottle and the old value is zero it subsequently calls SetInventoryValue(item,1), with PutItemOnSlot in between. This is conditional original caller order.",
    "ScriptCommand_GetInventoryValue and ScriptCommand_SetInventoryValue are separate handlers whose order is chosen by the original script stream. No mandatory write-then-read transaction or authored forced schedule is admitted."
  ],
  "originalhostprerequisites": [
    "Original gSave.inventory backing accessible at0x02002b32..0x02002b71 during synchronous invocation.",
    "Qualification itemIDs0..255 and writevalues0..3; complete caller domains/save-load schedule remain open.",
    "No concurrent/interrupt observer of mechanical full-bank writeback is covered."
  ],
